WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.300
- On today's episode it's a
hotbed of Hollywood hunkery.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.520
But who is the biggest Hollywood hotshot?

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.660
Brad versus Leo.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.230
They're currently on top in Tinseltown.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.760
And this epic matchup takes place

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.933
once upon a time in Hollywood.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.070
It's the name of their movie.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.080
- Cut.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:17.913
- You embarrassed yourself like that

00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:20.500
in front of all them goddamn people.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.350
- Anyway.
Here's how it works.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.830
Round one, box office.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.830
Round two, tomatometer.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.660
Round three, awards.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.180
And we'll do a wildcard round.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.200
Then you will determine the winner.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.070
One will continue to be an A-list actor,

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.640
and the other is doomed to a fate

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.500
of summer stock forever more.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.490
Let's get it on.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:40.392
- I got a six pack in the back,
thought we'd order a pizza.

00:00:40.392 --> 00:00:41.225
- [Leo] All right.

00:00:41.225 --> 00:00:42.910
- Round one, box office.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:44.940
Brad Pitt has had a
longer career than Leo,

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.350
and has accrued more total
dollars at the Cineplex,

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.300
so does that mean he wins this round?

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.683
Or is he just older?

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.160
- Web of lies.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.860
- Brad's lifetime domestic
haul stands at $4.29 billion.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.999
While Leo's is $3.64 billion.

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:01.690
Let's take a closer look.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.300
Without Pitt's eight
second cameo in Deadpool 2,

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.440
that total number for him
slides down to $3.98 billion.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:11.287
And Leo has a much
higher per movie average.

00:01:11.287 --> 00:01:15.510
$152 million for him,
$110 million for Brad.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.760
So is it quantity over quality?

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.330
If you're asking me about french fries,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.523
the answer's always yes.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.750
When it comes to movies, I like a fella

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.790
who has a guaranteed smash hit every time.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.860
Brad has made 39 flicks,
and some real gems in there.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.950
But Leo, he's only done 24 movies

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.020
and he throws a haymaker with
every new talkie he releases.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.460
I did the math, somebody
here did the math,

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.920
and by the time Leo is 60, and Brad Pitt

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.920
has turned into a little wrinkly baby,

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.790
DiCaprio will overtake
him at the box office.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.140
So DiCaprio wins the round.
(dinging)

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.390
And he's up one nothing.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.417
- I'm the king of the world.

00:01:54.318 --> 00:01:55.151
Woo!

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.580
- Round two, tomatometer.

00:01:58.580 --> 00:01:59.940
Well if it's quality you want,

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.460
look no further than the caliber of film

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.033
these gentlemen put out.

00:02:05.952 --> 00:02:07.340
(speaking foreign language)

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.010
They're both the rare actor that can brag

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:12.240
about having a career fresh
average on the tomatometer.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.100
Brad's films rates 64.5% on average.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.920
Leo trails him by only a
couple points, at 62.8%.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.020
Both these fellas tie for

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:23.790
highest individual movie score, at 95%.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.800
Brad earned his for 12 Years a Slave.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.700
Leo for Catch Me if you Can.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.000
- [Woman] Would you like
a drink after takeoff?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.010
- Milk?

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.300
- Brad wasn't the star of his movie,

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.770
but he did produce it and
he won an Oscar for it.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:35.970
- It is a fact.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.810
A plain and simple fact.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:40.270
That what is true and right
is true and right for all.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:43.000
- So what are the films that
are weighing the boys down?

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.990
Well Leo has a big fat
goose egg on his resume,

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.530
that being for Critters 3.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.000
- You can't expect us to
believe this horseshit.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.320
- It's at 0%.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.322
That's not his fault, he was like nine.

00:02:53.322 --> 00:02:55.170
(gurgling)

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.560
Brad's lowest is 4% for Cool World.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.300
And I am shocked it took me that long

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.630
to reference that classic.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.185
Remember Cool World?

00:03:02.185 --> 00:03:04.850
(thunking and chuckling)

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.770
That 4% would be a lot higher if

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.310
Who Framed Roger Rabbit
hadn't already come out.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.870
No?
I'm getting the word no,

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.188
that apparently that
movie's still terrible.

00:03:13.188 --> 00:03:15.200
(laughing)

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.740
This round comes down to who's been

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.080
doing it better for longer.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.600
I got Pitt by the slightest
of margins in both regards.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:22.916
Brad ekes out a victory in this round.

00:03:22.916 --> 00:03:23.749
(dinging)

00:03:23.749 --> 00:03:24.860
And we're tied at one a piece.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.907
- 'Cause business is a booming.

00:03:26.907 --> 00:03:28.290
(laughing)

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.500
- Round three, awards.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.200
Look movies are fun and all.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.980
But we know they're not worth anything

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.560
unless they win a trophy.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.940
Same goes for actors.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.800
And both these studs have
built quite a resume.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.650
Brad Pitt, you know how many
total awards this guy has won?

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.220
67!

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.053
67.

00:03:45.053 --> 00:03:46.500
He's two away from Bill and Ted's

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.010
favorite number of all time.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.440
- 69, dudes.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:54.290
- And he's been nominated 152 times.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.112
The guy from Cool World has won 67 awards.

00:03:57.112 --> 00:03:58.990
(laughing)

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:01.750
Well good luck competing
in this category, Leo.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:02.970
I'm sorry, what's that?

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.510
Boys and girls I'm just getting word,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.750
Leonardo DiCaprio has won 97 awards.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:12.340
And he's been nominated 209 times.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.420
So he has more nominations, more wins,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.160
and a better nom to win ratio than Brad.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.650
But how about with the important awards?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.410
There's one ceremony that stands

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.480
head and shoulders above the others.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.670
However, each fellow is tied
with four MTV Movie Awards.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.170
So let's go to the lowly Oscars instead.

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:31.220
Leo finally took home Oscar gold

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.760
with his win for The Revenant.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.470
Two years before, Brad got his first Oscar

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.270
for producing 12 Years a Slave.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.260
So they're tied with one win apiece,

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:41.440
and six nominations each.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.630
But, Leo's have all come from acting.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.070
Brad has nominated thrice for acting,

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:48.680
thrice for producing.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.450
And what are we talking about here today?

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:51.460
Movie stardom.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.470
Producing is great, like
you pick up a phone,

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.580
you say how are things going onset?

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:57.220
I'm sure more goes into it than that.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.860
But I'm giving the win to Leo
(dinging)

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.566
because he's won more times for acting.

00:05:01.566 --> 00:05:04.066
(goofy music)

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.280
Wild card round.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.710
Acting range.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:09.810
Yes acting range.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.530
Look, it's easy to be a leading man

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:12.540
when you're good looking,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.410
but which actor has the most range

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:17.400
when it comes to a roll, Brad or Leo?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.090
Leo first came to prominence playing

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.150
a mentally disabled teenager
in What's Eating Gilbert Grape.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.490
He would go on to play everything from

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:25.390
a drug addicted basketball player,

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:28.942
to a reclusive innovator,
to a maniac stockbroker.

00:05:28.942 --> 00:05:33.219
- So let's knock this
motherfucker outta the park!

00:05:33.219 --> 00:05:34.052
Oh!

00:05:34.052 --> 00:05:35.700
- And when he acts with Kate Winslet

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.955
he can either be a bored suburban husband,

00:05:37.955 --> 00:05:40.030
or really wet and cold.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.370
Good range, kid.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:43.380
But let me tell you something about Brad,

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:47.370
stoner, psychopath, cult
leader, bare knuckle boxer,

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:51.070
thief, outlaw, Nazi
hunter, and zombie slayer.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:52.850
And he can do all these
things while eating

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:55.670
a tremendous amount of calories onscreen.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:59.960
Pitt has consumed almost 5,000
calories onscreen, all told.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.723
Which is incidentally my
record at Golden Corral.

00:06:04.258 --> 00:06:05.920
(burping)

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.110
Leo does get points for
eating actual bison liver.

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:11.840
Like an actual bison liver, he ate it.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:14.110
And he was a damn good junior
thief in Growing Pains.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:15.450
Remember when he was on the TV show?

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.270
But the winner of the round is the man

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.460
who is possibly the
dumbest personal trainer

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:21.596
in the history of cinema, Mr. Brad Pitt.

00:06:21.596 --> 00:06:22.610
(dinging)

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.540
- Well like, you're so plugged into

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:25.530
the intelligence community.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.260
- So at the end of the wildcard round

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.930
we find ourselves in a dead heat.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:29.910
It's tied at two.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.590
So my tiebreaker will be
based purely on my gut.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:37.610
And my gut is saying, go with
the guy with the better abs.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:38.870
And this is no slight to Leo,

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:41.310
but have you seen Brad's six-pack?

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:43.240
Seriously, it's not even fair.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:45.530
The guy eats in every scene in every movie

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.130
he's ever been in, and
he still looks like that.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.420
- Ah, you sir, yeah you do the honors.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.283
- Brad gets the win as the
biggest Hollywood hotshot.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.240
- It's official old buddy.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:58.073
I'm a has been.

00:07:00.142 --> 00:07:01.730
- That's what losing sounds like.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.480
- But that's just my superficial take,

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.800
the real judge is you, the viewer.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.390
Head to the comment section right now,

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:09.220
and vote by telling us your winner.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:10.500
Is it the guy from The Beach,

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.340
or the dude from Tree of Life?

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:14.700
Good luck understanding
either one of those films.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.550
Thanks for tuning in.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:16.550
I'm Mark Ellis.

